        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r446400749-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Spiritual experience and reflection of life!",
        "text": "The Temple of Pashupatinath is dedicated to Lord Shiva, the Guardian Deity of Nepal. Pashupati means the Lord of all animate beings. This sacred place lies on the bank of River Bagmati and this area is called Deha Patan. With the main temple in the pagoda styled roof, it houses the Jyotir Linga / illuminating phallus which is surrounded by many other temples dedicated to different gods, goddesses and deities. There are two important moments in the temple: morning and evening aarati (offering the sacred candles to the deity and blessings by the priests). On the bank of the river the final death rituals are conducted. On the other side of the river are the temples dedicated to Lord Rama and walking up the Slesmantak forest you will visit the temples of Gorakhnatha, Hanumana, ganesha and the Vishwaroopa dedicated to the Universal representation of Lord Vishnu. On continuing the descend you will visit the other important Shakti Temple dedicated to Guheshwari. From here you can continue your journey on foot the the Stupa of Boudhanath! namaste",
        "review_tip": null,
