        "title": "Rites of Passage - Cremation by the holy river",
        "text": "A solemn and somber Tuesday. I witness three cremation. A big burly fair skin man, a petite small size lady and a medium size man sharedthe same final destiny. Death stings! The grief was indescribable as the son laid the father's body to a final rest.. For the Hindus, the karma and reincarnation worldview is deep and entwined with their culture. Where does the soul goes? Must go to understand the Nepali rites of Passage. ",
