        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r444604871-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Massive area, many temples, extremely crowded",
        "text": "The entire are covered by the Pashupatinath Temple is massive. It plays host to virtually every major ceremony in the lives of Hindus - naming ceremony of a child, marriages, cremations and post-death ceremonies - making it a hugely significant temple.\n\nEntry inside the main temple is restricted to Hindus only, and even as Hindus, it's not very easy to get the darshans from each of the four 'dwaars' (doors). There will be a lot of pushing, shoving and jostling for space, all of which has to be managed while taking good care of your belongings. We were lucky to have gotten the darshans from each door of the main temple and then we roamed around the other temples surrounding it in a relaxed manner.\n\nIf you hire a guide, they will explain the significance of many of these small temples and the stories surrounding them. More often than not, there will be a cremation ceremony in progress at the crematorium sites behind the temple along the river.\n\nIt is a huge place of great religious significance and worth a visit. The huge crowd does make it a somewhat chaotic experience, but a worthwhile one too.",
